        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T09:43:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e When adding SharedBufferMemory previously, I did not find a reason to track a secondary serial for shared buffers, so mLastSharedBufferUsageSerial doesn\u0027t exist. I think mLastUsageSerial is correct to use here.\n\nMy bad, I thought it was a new member but it is preexisting.\n\n\u003e I added code to optimize out the flush when EndAccess was called and Dawn did no work, which is what I think you meant here.\n\nWhile this works, now the fences returned in [1] won\u0027t necessarily have waited on whatever fences were passed in on BeginAccess if the buffer is never used. I don\u0027t remember exactly how STM handles that (or if it does), we should match it (even if it involves rolling back the patchset) for consistency.",
      "parentUuid": "f127145d_9d1641c7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 629,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 629,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "961e228418cf3327600dc370e3e9b3bf958fdd8e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
